children":"Fed minutes reveal a split among officials on interest-rate cuts, balancing concerns over rising unemployment with persistent inflation above the 2% target."}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"post-social","children":["$","ul",null,{"className":"social-list d-flex align-items-center","children":[["$","li",null,{}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://www.instagram.com/laur.enjacobs001/","className":"instagram","children":["$","i",null,{"className":"lab la-instagram"}]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://medium.com/@lauren_jacobs","className":"","style":{"border":""},"children":["$","i",null,{"className":"lab la-medium"}]}]}],["$","li",null,{"children":["$","$L11",null,{"href":"https://substack.com/@laurenjacobs672308","className":"pinterest","children":["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"20","height":"15","viewBox":"0 0 256 256","children":["$","g",null,{"transform":"scale(5.12,5.12)","children":[["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,11h-35v-6h35z"}],["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,19h-35v-6h35z"}],["$","path",null,{"d":"M43,44.805l-17.016,-10.636l-17.984,10.579v-23.748h35z"}]]}]}]}]}]]}]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"row","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"col-lg-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"post-layout-content","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"layout-thumb mb-30","children":["$","$L12",null,{"title":"Fed minutes: Most officials supported further rate cuts as worries about jobs rose","src":"/images/fed-rate-cut-debate.webp","alt":"Fed minutes: Most officials supported further rate cuts as worries about jobs rose","width":1200,"height":800,"priority":true,"style":{"width":"100%","height":"auto"}}]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"layout-desc","style":{"marginBottom":"1rem"},"children":"Most members of the Federal Reserve’s interest-rate setting committee supported further reductions to its key interest rate this year, according to minutes from last month’s meeting released Wednesday.  A majority of Fed officials felt that the risk unemployment would rise had worsened since their previous meeting in July, while the risk of rising inflation “had either diminished or not increased,” the minutes said.  As a result, the central bank decided at its Sept.  16-17 meeting to reduce its key rate by a quarter-point to about 4. 1%, its first cut this year.  Rate cuts by the Fed can gradually lower borrowing costs for things like mortgages, auto loans, and business loans, encouraging more spending and hiring."}],"$L13","$L14","$L15"]}],"$L16","$L17"]}]}],"$L18"]}]]}]}],"$L19"]}]}]]
